# Playwright — Cursor enforcement

**Canonical runbook:** `AGENTS.md` — read it before editing or generating Playwright files.

**Cursor workflows:** `.cursor/workflows/*.md`

## Enforce (summary — full detail in AGENTS.md)

- Import `test` / `expect` from `@fixtures` (`src/fixtures/test.fixture.ts`), not `@playwright/test`.
- Register Page Objects in `test.fixture.ts`. Specs must never use `new PageObject(page)`.
- Selectors: accessibility-first (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, then `getByTestId` / `data-qa`). No raw CSS/XPath.
- POMs extend `BasePage` in `src/pages/base.page.ts`; no locators in spec files.
- Tags: `@smoke` or `@regression` in every test title; CI gate is smoke only.
- WIP tests: `test.skip()` with reason — never commit failing regression.
- Credentials from env via `TEST_CREDENTIALS` / `API_CONFIG`; never hardcode secrets.

## After generating or changing tests

1. Run `npm run typecheck && npm run test:smoke` when feasible.
2. On failure: use test-analyzer MCP on `test-results/report.json`.

## Do not duplicate standards here

If AGENTS.md and this rule conflict, **AGENTS.md wins**.
